WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.601
-Welcome back
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:02.601 --> 00:00:04.968
I'm Steve Higgins, and we're
about to play "Pup Quiz."

00:00:04.968 --> 00:00:05.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.968 --> 00:00:08.334
♪♪

00:00:08.334 --> 00:00:13.801
[ Dogs barking ]

00:00:13.801 --> 00:00:15.534
Aww.

00:00:15.534 --> 00:00:17.834
Playing tonight, we have
the host of "The Tonight Show,"

00:00:17.834 --> 00:00:19.400
Mr. Jimmy Fallon.

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:22.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:22.133 --> 00:00:24.133
Oh.
And his opponent,

00:00:24.133 --> 00:00:26.133
the star of
"John Wick: Chapter 4,"

00:00:26.133 --> 00:00:30.934
premiering in theaters and IMAX
March 24th, Keanu Reeves.

00:00:30.934 --> 00:00:32.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:32.634 --> 00:00:34.501
Aww.

00:00:34.501 --> 00:00:36.100
Okay.

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:38.200
This is the first puppy
up tonight.

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:40.300
Named Gary Frick Jr.

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:42.467
[ Audience "Awws" ]

00:00:42.467 --> 00:00:43.701
And here's how it's gonna work.

00:00:43.701 --> 00:00:46.434
I'll be asking both of you
animal trivia questions.

00:00:46.434 --> 00:00:47.567
[ Audience "Awws" ]

00:00:47.567 --> 00:00:49.667
And if you answer correctly,

00:00:49.667 --> 00:00:51.834
you will receive
a golden retriever puppy.

00:00:51.834 --> 00:00:53.400
[ Audience "Awws" ]

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:54.834
-That's the way it works.

00:00:54.834 --> 00:00:59.033
-If you answer incorrectly,
your opponent gets the puppy.

00:00:59.033 --> 00:01:02.868
And whoever has the most puppies
at the end of the game

00:01:02.868 --> 00:01:04.367
is the Pup Quiz champion.

00:01:04.367 --> 00:01:06.968
Keanu, since you're our guest,
you'll answer the first question

00:01:06.968 --> 00:01:10.868
and either win or lose
Mr. Gary Frick Jr.

00:01:10.868 --> 00:01:12.234
-Okay.

00:01:12.234 --> 00:01:15.100
-What is the only species
of reptile --

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:16.801
-I'm so terrible with this.

00:01:16.801 --> 00:01:18.133
[ Laughter ]
-Wait.

00:01:18.133 --> 00:01:19.434
He didn't even finish
the question.

00:01:19.434 --> 00:01:22.167
-I know. I just know it's just
gonna be a disaster.

00:01:22.167 --> 00:01:24.634
-No, come on.
-It's just -- go ahead.

00:01:24.634 --> 00:01:25.934
-You're gonna get this one.

00:01:25.934 --> 00:01:29.033
What is the only species
of reptile native to Ireland.

00:01:29.033 --> 00:01:31.167
Is it, A, snake...
-Come on.

00:01:31.167 --> 00:01:34.200
-...B, lizard, or, C, turtle?

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:36.434
Not sea turtle.
C, turtle.

00:01:36.434 --> 00:01:38.300
-Native to Ireland.

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:39.767
Okay.
So all of those are kind of,

00:01:39.767 --> 00:01:41.400
like, the thing and what's
gonna be the thing,

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:43.200
and then what's the thing that
you don't think it's gonna be,

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:45.200
so you're gonna say turtle.
-Right.

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:47.067
But then you're gonna
change your answer to...

00:01:47.067 --> 00:01:48.734
-Uh, uh, lizard.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.734 --> 00:01:50.667
-Lizard. Yes!

00:01:50.667 --> 00:01:55.067
Lizard is correct!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:55.067 --> 00:01:59.434
You win Gary Frick Jr.
-Hey, buddy.

00:01:59.434 --> 00:02:02.133
-Come on.

00:02:02.133 --> 00:02:03.734
This is not fair.
First of all,

00:02:03.734 --> 00:02:06.367
I'm not taking a puppy
away from John Wick.

00:02:06.367 --> 00:02:07.834
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.834 --> 00:02:10.334
Just saying that right now.
-Okay.

00:02:10.334 --> 00:02:12.133
This next question's for you,
Jimmy.

00:02:12.133 --> 00:02:13.634
-Okay.
-Where you going?

00:02:13.634 --> 00:02:15.534
-Which of the following species

00:02:15.534 --> 00:02:17.567
is not the name
of a real animal?

00:02:17.567 --> 00:02:19.067
Okay?
Which of the following

00:02:19.067 --> 00:02:21.267
is not the name
of a real animal species?

00:02:21.267 --> 00:02:25.367
Is it, A, sarcastic fringehead,

00:02:25.367 --> 00:02:29.567
B, spiny lumpsucker,

00:02:29.567 --> 00:02:31.467
or, C, shorty bobbit.

00:02:31.467 --> 00:02:33.801
-The following is not the name
of a real animal species.

00:02:33.801 --> 00:02:36.601
I think it's
sarcastic fringehead.

00:02:36.601 --> 00:02:39.801
-Sarcastic fringehead.
Is that your final answer?

00:02:39.801 --> 00:02:41.133
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:02:41.133 --> 00:02:42.200
-It is?
-Yeah.

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:45.167
-No!
Answer was shorty bobbit.

00:02:45.167 --> 00:02:47.267
Oh, shorty bobbit.
[ Audience "Ohs" ]

00:02:47.267 --> 00:02:53.267
Now Keanu wins the adorable
puppy, Mary Kennedy.

00:02:53.267 --> 00:02:56.200
-Oh.
Do they know each other?

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:59.367
Do the puppies know each other?
Is this, like, a common litter?

00:02:59.367 --> 00:03:00.901
-We have like
50 puppies backstage.

00:03:00.901 --> 00:03:03.868
[ Laughter ]
-You got Gary and Mary.

00:03:03.868 --> 00:03:06.000
[ Dog barking ]
Oh, my gosh! Do you hear that?

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:07.267
-No.
-That sound means it's time

00:03:07.267 --> 00:03:08.901
for Double Puppardy.
-Oh.

00:03:08.901 --> 00:03:10.000
[ Laughter ]
-Double Puppardy?

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:12.234
-Questions are now worth
two puppies.

00:03:12.234 --> 00:03:13.200
[ Laughter ]
-Watch out.

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:14.367
-Keanu.
-What?

00:03:14.367 --> 00:03:16.968
-A dik-dik...
[ Laughter ]

00:03:16.968 --> 00:03:19.934
A dik-dik is what kind
of animal?

00:03:19.934 --> 00:03:23.334
Is it, A, platypus --
A platypus.

00:03:23.334 --> 00:03:28.434
B, is for bird, or C, antelope,
not cantaloupe.

00:03:28.434 --> 00:03:29.801
[ Laughter ]

00:03:29.801 --> 00:03:32.267
-Okay. So, you do the one
that you think it's gonna be,

00:03:32.267 --> 00:03:34.367
but then you pick the one that
you don't think it's gonna be,

00:03:34.367 --> 00:03:36.434
and then you pick the one that
you don't think it's gonna be,

00:03:36.434 --> 00:03:38.934
and then the dik-dik
is an antelope.

00:03:38.934 --> 00:03:40.601
-That is correct!
[ Ding! ]

00:03:40.601 --> 00:03:42.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:43.667
-Are you out of your mind?

00:03:43.667 --> 00:03:48.267
-Keanu, you and Lisa McAdams
and Lisa Armstrong.

00:03:48.267 --> 00:03:51.968
-Double Puppardy.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:51.968 --> 00:03:55.067
-Wow.
-Let's go, Fallon.

00:03:55.067 --> 00:03:57.434
-Come here, boy.
That's it. Come here, boy.

00:03:57.434 --> 00:03:58.901
That's a good boy.
-It's puppy love!

00:03:58.901 --> 00:04:00.701
-You give that one back --

00:04:00.701 --> 00:04:02.934
-That's my puppy, Fallon!

00:04:02.934 --> 00:04:04.234
-I love it.
-All right, next question

00:04:04.234 --> 00:04:05.567
goes to Jimmy.

00:04:05.567 --> 00:04:08.367
Why do males dogs raise their
leg when is they urinate?

00:04:08.367 --> 00:04:09.434
[ Laughter ]

00:04:09.434 --> 00:04:12.868
Is it, A, to tell others
they are tall?

00:04:12.868 --> 00:04:15.767
Is it, B, to tell other dogs
they are happy?

00:04:15.767 --> 00:04:19.701
Or it is, C, to tell other dogs
they are DTF.

00:04:19.701 --> 00:04:20.934
[ Laughter ]

00:04:20.934 --> 00:04:23.968
Down to fetch.
Down to fetch.

00:04:23.968 --> 00:04:26.567
-Maybe, uh, B?
-No, it's to tell other dogs

00:04:26.567 --> 00:04:28.100
they are tall.
[ Sad tuba ]

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:31.267
So, Keanu, you get Roger Blaine
and Ted Mooney.

00:04:31.267 --> 00:04:32.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:32.601 --> 00:04:33.801
♪♪

00:04:33.801 --> 00:04:36.767
-Can you help the dogs?

00:04:36.767 --> 00:04:38.067
-Hi.

00:04:38.067 --> 00:04:40.601
-Who's the puppy king?
-Come here.

00:04:40.601 --> 00:04:42.501
There you go.
-I'm the puppy king!

00:04:42.501 --> 00:04:43.934
-There we go.
He's got 'em.

00:04:43.934 --> 00:04:46.067
-There we go.
All right.

00:04:46.067 --> 00:04:48.300
[ Laughs ]
-Hey, buddy.

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:49.501
-Okay.

00:04:49.501 --> 00:04:51.834
[ Dog barking ]
Oh, my gosh!

00:04:51.834 --> 00:04:54.634
That sound means it's time
for Final Puppardy.

00:04:54.634 --> 00:04:57.567
This is for all your opponent's
puppies and the game.

00:04:57.567 --> 00:04:59.400
So pick up your iPads
if you can.

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:00.868
[ Laughter ]

00:05:00.868 --> 00:05:05.601
How many dogs were used
to film the movie "Air Bud"?

00:05:05.601 --> 00:05:07.067
All right.
You'll have 10 seconds

00:05:07.067 --> 00:05:08.634
on the clock starting now.

00:05:08.634 --> 00:05:11.000
[ Laughter ]

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:12.934
-Okay.

00:05:12.934 --> 00:05:15.334
[ Laughter ]

00:05:15.334 --> 00:05:17.033
-They left, they left.
They just left.

00:05:17.033 --> 00:05:18.067
They left.
-Oh!

00:05:18.067 --> 00:05:19.400
-They left, okay?
They're wandering --

00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:20.400
[ Buzzer ]

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:22.200
It's chaos.
I'm gonna say 10.

00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:23.567
-Keanu, what did you write down?

00:05:23.567 --> 00:05:26.667
-Uh, 6, but if it's not 6,
then it's a 9.

00:05:26.667 --> 00:05:28.801
[ Laughter ]

00:05:28.801 --> 00:05:30.367
-The answer is 6!

00:05:30.367 --> 00:05:32.667
[ Ding! ]
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:32.667 --> 00:05:35.033
-There we go.

00:05:35.033 --> 00:05:38.767
My thanks to Keanu Reeves,
these adorable puppies.

00:05:38.767 --> 00:05:41.200
Stick around! We'll be right
back with Melanie Lynskey!

00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:42.968
Congratulations.

00:05:42.968 --> 00:05:46.968
-How's it going?
Yeah.

